  "tagline": "Fast distributed SQL query engine for federated analytics across lakes and databases.",
  "description": "Trino is the open-source MPP SQL engine created by Presto's original authors when they forked PrestoSQL in 2019 (renamed in 2020). Like Presto it stores nothing itself: it queries Iceberg, Delta Lake, Hudi and Hive tables on object storage and federates over dozens of connectors, from PostgreSQL to Elasticsearch to Kafka. It has become the default open lakehouse query engine, with strong Iceberg support (DML, time travel, materialized views) and fault-tolerant execution for longer ETL. It needs a well-sized cluster and good file layout to perform; Starburst and Amazon Athena provide managed versions.",
